cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RIFT in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "RIFT: Intervention-Grounded Detection of Behavioral Divergence"
version: "0.1.0-phase4"
date-released: "2026-08-17"
abstract: >
  RIFT is a research prototype for causal attribution of behavioral divergence
  in distributed microservice systems. It combines causal discovery (FCI/PAG),
  explicit do-calculus intervention semantics, Wasserstein-based divergence
  analysis (CID), earliest behavioral divergence detection (EBD), and
  closed-loop Bayesian graph updates into one experimental pipeline.
  Designed for empirical evaluation on the Online Boutique microservice testbed
  with real tc/netem fault injection.
authors:
  - family-names: Sakthivel
    given-names: Manas
repository-code: "https://github.com/ManasSakthivel/RIFT-Intervention-Grounded-Detection-of-Behavioral-Divergence"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - root cause analysis
  - distributed systems
  - microservices
  - fault injection
  - causal discovery
  - FCI
  - behavioral divergence
  - intervention
  - do-calculus
